    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30804" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐθν-άρχης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ruler of a tribe</i> or <i>nation</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄσανδρος ἀντὶ ἐθνάρχου βασιλεὺς
					ἀναγορευθεὶς βοσπόρου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Macr.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			; <i>sheikh</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				616.2
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Arabia</span>); of Abraham, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.513
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> title of
			Jewish official, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ma.</u>
				14.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.1.13
			</span></i>, Nic.Dam.<i><span class="en">
				p.143
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">D., <u>2
				Ep.Cor.</u>11.32</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				13.6.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj., <i>ruling over nations</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. θεοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Gal.</u>
					115d
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				143a
			</span></i>.</div>
